  "title": "The Communist Manifesto",
  "summary": "In February 1848 the Manifesto of the Communist Party, written by Karl Marx and Friedrich Engels for the Communist League, was first published; its manuscript went to London for printing a few weeks before that month's French revolution. It calls history the history of class struggles, declares the bourgeoisie's fall and the proletariat's victory equally inevitable, and ends by calling on working men of all countries to unite.",
